"privacy": ["Privacy policy", "Who operates Matchday\nMatchday is operated by Muhammad Saran Khalid. For privacy questions, contact muhammadsarankhalid@gmail.com. Effective 14 September 2026.", "Information we use\nWe process your sign-in email and account ID, profile name, username and photos; optional profile and cricket details; team memberships, invitations, fixtures, scores and tournament records; posts, comments, messages and images you submit; follows, blocks, reports and notification preferences. If you choose location features, we use the location you enter or permit your device to provide. We use device push tokens to deliver notifications. Our hosting and authentication providers may process network information such as IP addresses and request logs for operation and security.", "Why we use it\nWe use this information to provide accounts, organize cricket, show scorecards, deliver messages and notifications, respond to support requests, and investigate abuse. Matchday does not include advertising or sell personal data. Optional photos, location access and notifications can be declined; some related features will then be unavailable.", "Who can see it\nProfiles, public posts, teams and match records can be visible to other users. Messages are presented to chat participants. Uploaded images are served using hosted URLs; anyone who receives an image URL may be able to open or retain a copy. Do not upload sensitive documents or confidential images. Other users may keep screenshots or copies of content you share.", "Service providers and transfers\nWe use Supabase for authentication, databases, file storage and backend services; Google sign-in and Firebase Cloud Messaging for authentication and push notifications; and location/search providers when those features are used. Data may be processed outside Pakistan. The support website is hosted through OpenAI Sites and its infrastructure providers. Network connections use HTTPS. Messages are not end-to-end encrypted.", "Retention and deletion\nAccount information is kept while your account remains active. Settings \u2192 Delete account removes your account, personal profile, authored posts and comments, follows, push tokens and uploaded files. Messages you sent are replaced with deletion notices. Shared cricket scorecards can remain with your account identity removed and the label Deleted player. Team ownership may transfer to another manager, or the team may be archived. Copies held by other users and provider backup/security retention are not instantly erased by deletion. Contact us for a specific data-removal request or questions about provider retention.", "Your choices\nYou can edit your profile, manage notifications, report content, block users and delete your account in Settings. You can also request deletion without installing the app through the Delete account page on this website. We verify ownership before acting on an email request. Do not send passwords, one-time codes or identity documents in your request.", "Adults and changes\nMatchday\u2019s initial release is intended for adults aged 18 or older. If you believe a child has provided personal information, contact us for review and removal. We update this page when our practices change and show the effective date above."],
"terms": ["Terms and community standards", "Using Matchday\nMatchday helps adult cricket players and organizers manage teams, matches and community activity. By using Matchday, you confirm you are at least 18 and agree to these terms. Provide accurate account information and keep access to your sign-in account secure.", "Your content\nOnly upload content you have the right to share. Obtain permission before sharing another person\u2019s contact information or photos. You retain your rights and permit Matchday to store, display and deliver your content to provide the service.", "Prohibited conduct\nDo not post or send harassment, threats, hate speech, sexual exploitation, child sexual abuse material, non-consensual intimate content, spam, impersonation, scams, illegal content, or material that infringes someone else\u2019s rights. Do not use Matchday to arrange harmful or illegal activity, attack the service or bypass another user\u2019s block.", "Reports and enforcement\nUse the options menu on a profile, post, comment or message to report abuse or block a user. Reports are reviewed by the Matchday operator. We may remove content, restrict an account or suspend access for violations. Child exploitation is prohibited; suspected child sexual abuse material will be removed and reported to the appropriate authorities as required by applicable law. Child safety and moderation contact: muhammadsarankhalid@gmail.com. For immediate danger, contact local emergency services.", "Cricket and availability\nOrganizers are responsible for venue permission, participant safety and match arrangements. Check scorecards and arrangements with your team. Service interruptions and scoring mistakes can occur; Matchday does not guarantee uninterrupted availability or replace official competition rules.", "Access and support\nThe initial release is free and has no advertising or paid features. You can stop using the service and request account deletion at any time. For support or to appeal moderation, contact muhammadsarankhalid@gmail.com. Nothing in these terms limits rights that cannot legally be excluded."],
"delete-account": ["Delete your Matchday account", "Delete in the app\nOpen Matchday \u2192 menu \u2192 Settings \u2192 Delete account. Read the consequences, type DELETE and confirm. Keep the app open while deletion completes. If a network error interrupts deletion, retry or contact support; some uploaded files may already have been removed.", "Request deletion without the app\nEmail muhammadsarankhalid@gmail.com from the address used for your Matchday account with the subject \u201cDelete my Matchday account\u201d. Include your username if you know it. If your Google sign-in uses a different address, tell us which account you want removed. We will verify ownership before deletion. Never send a password or one-time sign-in code. The email link below opens your email app; send the message there to submit your request.", "What is deleted\nYour sign-in account and personal profile, authored posts and comments, follows, notification tokens and uploaded files are removed. Messages you sent are replaced with deletion notices. Shared cricket records may remain with your account identity removed, labeled Deleted player. Shared teams can transfer to a remaining manager or be archived.", "What can remain\nPeople who received your content may have their own copies. Provider backups and security logs follow the providers\u2019 retention practices and may not disappear immediately. Ask support about a particular retained item. Account deletion cannot be undone."],
